Data provenance
crates/unityrs-core/src/typetree/commonstring.rs: the 108 common strings
of UnityPy 1.25.2's MIT source (UnityPy/enums/CommonString.py). The table
UnityPy's blob parser reads is its type-tree package's, which unityrs builds
at run time from the package the user supplies; nothing from a package is
committed.

crates/unityrs-core/src/classid.rs: class id names generated from
UnityPy 1.25.2's MIT UnityPy/enums/ClassIDType.py.

crates/unityrs-core/src/tables.rs: the zero of every decimal-digit (Nd) run,
the code points whose lower case differs between Python 3.11 and Rust, and
the two classes that decide a capital sigma's final form (Cased and
Case_Ignorable, as Final_Sigma reads them), generated from Python 3.11's
unicodedata and str.lower() (Unicode 14.0.0, from the Unicode Character
Database) and the pinned Rust toolchain's char::to_lowercase.

crates/unityrs-dump/src/select/printable.rs: the code points Python 3.11's
str.isprintable() refuses (the general categories Cc, Cf, Cs, Co, Cn, Zl,
Zp and Zs but the space), generated from Python 3.11 (Unicode 14.0.0, from
the Unicode Character Database).

The Unicode License v3 text, which covers the Unicode data in both, is
listed under Crates below.

No type-tree package (TPK) file is included in this repository or in any
binary built from it. unityrs-tpk loads one from a path the user supplies.
The TPK tests read
synthetic packages built in code (tools/fixtures/tpk.py) and, in the oracle
image only, UnityPy's own package, from which nothing is committed.

No game data is included in this repository. Test inputs are synthetic and
built in code.

